Template method lets you define the general structure of an algorithm while deferring
the implementation of certain steps to subclasses.

It is a behavioral design pattern the defines the skeleton of an algorithm in a base class.
allowing subclasses to redefine specific steps without changing the algorithms structure.

Template vs Strategy

Template emphasis within a common framework , allowing subclasses to override parts of
the process as needed. It focuses on a fixed process rather than choosing between
different algo's.

The stratergy pattern emphasis the interchangeability of algos.IT allows you to choose between
different algos implemetation at runtime without affacting the structure of algo.

The stratergy pattern encapsulates each implmentation in separate classes ,  making them interchangeable in
through interfaces, while template method achieves partial customizaton through inheritence.

when to use:

When have a general process that needs to be shared among multiple classes but certain steps need
to be customised based on specific requirements.

